  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive. The transitive counterpart is {定|さだ}める (to determine, to establish, to set).\n\nGodan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), る-ending.\n- Negative: {定|さだ}まらない\n- Polite: {定|さだ}まります\n- Te-form: {定|さだ}まって\n- Past: {定|さだ}まった\n\nUSAGE:\nSomewhat literary or formal. In everyday speech, {決|き}まる is more common for \"to be decided.\" {定|さだ}まる implies a more gradual or authoritative settling of something — a policy taking shape, a reputation becoming established, or conditions stabilizing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {方針|ほうしん}が{定|さだ}まる: the policy is decided\n- {評価|ひょうか}が{定|さだ}まる: the evaluation is established\n- {心|こころ}が{定|さだ}まる: one's mind is made up\n- {天候|てんこう}が{定|さだ}まらない: the weather won't settle",
